    "____OUTLIERS:\n",
    "-Emperical rule - 68-95-99.7 rule. IT will be used to identify the outliers.\n",
    "-If any data point going above the standard deviation 99.7% range then we will call it as outliers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "389bdf63-1037-4c0e-b0ad-0b3c12190522",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "__Different types of graphs: \n",
    "-When the tale of the graph is growing in postivie direction it is called positively skewed.(IQR will be used to identify the outliers)\n",
    "-When it is grwoing in negative direction then it is negatively skewed.(IQR will be used to identify the outliers)\n",
    "-When the tail of the graph is growing on both positve and negative ends.(it may have positive or negative outliers that can be identified by using standard deviation)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "49bc0fbe-a3c8-44a2-b000-2f236a10eb1f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "___GRAPHS:\n",
    "-Tail of the graph- growing ends of the graph.\n",
    "-Kurtosis- peak of the graph.\n",
    "-Negatively skewed - when tail is growing in negative direction and curve in positive direction.\n",
    "-Positively skewed- when tail is growing in positive direction and curve in negative direction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "fa780f63-7944-4893-a6c4-622514cbec4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "___IQR: used for skewed data only.\n",
    "- Full form: Inter Quartiel Range.\n",
    "- Make quaters Q1, Q2 and Q3.\n",
    "- Q2 is the median of the data.\n",
    "- To calculate IQR perfrom Q3 - Q1 = x.\n",
    "- for upperfence of boxplot = Q3+1.5IQR\n",
    "                                Q3+1.5x\n",
    "- For lowerfence of boxplot = Q3-1.5x"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "47d0e0d5-0be6-42c7-8abf-7308cf50096f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "___JUDGEMENT IF DATA SET CONTAINS THE OUTLIERS:\n",
    "1. kde- it this graph has a perfect bell shape with not tails thens it does not have any outliers.\n",
    "2. boxplot- any value above the upperfence and below the lowerfence will be called as outliers. The values will be calculated by using IQR."
   ]
  }
